    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "0a85afc09924ba5ea29f96ea1d29fd18",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1520,
    "chunk_text": "We give priority to enhancing national productivity by strengthening education, competency development, research, innovation and digital transformation, modernizing public services, expanding digital infrastructure, encouraging the use of new technologies and strengthening collaboration among educational institutions, research institutions and industries.\n\n2.4 Empowering the Rural Economy and Ensuring Inclusive Growth\n\nThe agri-food sector has very high potential for export and rural income growth. Instead of excessive reliance on broad-based and untargeted subsidies that do not contribute to raising productivity, high priority should be given to directing unproductive lands to productive cultivation, agricultural research, climate-smart technology, water management, storage and cold storage facilities, product quality certification and digital systems. It is also essential to resolve, after proper study, the existing barriers to land use, rural access to finance and connecting producers to markets. Then, it will be possible to make the empowerment of the livelihoods of rural people, food security and foreign exchange earnings the outcomes of a single development process.\n\nA new economic transformation at the rural level can be brought about by encouraging small and medium-scale entrepreneurs, creating new economic opportunities for rural people, and developing the technical, vocational and linguistic skills required for the modern job market.\n\n2.5 Stability and Continuity of the Energy\n\nMarkets"
