    "chunk_text": "Hon. Speaker, digital transformation is no longer merely a technological initiative, but a fundamental requirement for improving the efficiency of the public sector, strengthening governance, facilitating economic growth and ensuring that every citizen can access Government services. Digitalization has been identified as a fundamental tool for modernizing public administration, improving the efficiency and transparency of Government activities and strengthening institutional capacity.\n\n\u2022 The GovTech institution has been established under\n\n100 per cent ownership of the Treasury to guide and implement the digitalization of public services, and has already commenced its operations.\n\n\u2022 The Personal Data Protection Act has been amended\n\nand the Data Protection Authority has already been established and made operational.\n\n\u2022 The Bill for the establishment of the Digital\n\nEconomy Authority and the National Digital Economy Council - Digital Economy Bill - is expected to be passed in the first quarter of 2027.\n\n\u2022 The Cyber Security Bill, which is essential for\n\nprotection with the growth of the digital sector, has been submitted to the Attorney-General for clearance. Accordingly, it is expected to establish a Cyber Security Authority under it in 2027.\n\n\u2022 There is a problematic situation in the Government\n\nprocurement process when purchasing digital solutions and facilities. Therefore, Government P rocurement Guidelines specific to digital solutions and facilities have been prepared, and discussions have already commenced with the Procurement Commission. Accordingly, it will be possible to introduce these procurement guidelines in the first half of 2027.\n\nFor a new transformation in the digital economy sector;\n\n\u2022 Establishing a National Artificial Intelligence Centre\n\nof Excellence at Wijerama Mawatha, bringing the Government, the expert community and industry under one roof to build national AI capabilities and promote the responsible use of AI;"
