    "chunk_text": "\u2022 Establishing a National Artificial Intelligence Centre\n\nof Excellence at Wijerama Mawatha, bringing the Government, the expert community and industry under one roof to build national AI capabilities and promote the responsible use of AI;\n\nBefore Build Policy\", which, in parallel with the standard for integrating public institutions through digital public infrastructure, gives priority to purchasing standardized solutions and to shared use, before developing new software in software procurement;\n\n363 364\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd4\u0dbb \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0db8\u0ddc\u0dbb \u0daf\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0ddc \u0ddc\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0ddc ]\n\n2026 \u0db1 \u0ddc\u0dc0\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 12\n\n\u2022 Expanding the Lanka Government Cloud \u2013 LGC -\n\nsystem from LGC 2.0 to LGC 3.0 and establishing the core foundation of sovereign infrastructure for Artificial Intelligence;\n\n\u2022 Digitalizing the services provided by Divisional\n\nSecretariats and Grama Niladharis so that citizens can easily access Government services;\n\n\u2022 Launching the \"Presidential Digital Excellence\n\nAwards\" programme to appriase high-performing public institutions with the aim of rapidly promoting digitalization;\n\n\u2022 Adopting and expanding cashless payment methods\n\nsuch as GovPay and QR to steer towards a digital revenue economy;\n\n\u2022 Further, preparing the necessary regulatory basis for\n\nVirtual Asset Service Providers \u2013 VASP - through the establishment of a formal legal framework;\n\n\u2022 Preparing sectoral digital plans to align the\n\ndigitalization of key strategic sectors with the National Digital Economy Plan, and carrying out operations through institutional Digital Transformation Units - DTUs;\n\n\u2022 Providing electricity tariff concessions and other\n\nincentives to encourage investors selected under formal criteria, with the expectation of encouraging investment in the establishment of data centres;\n\n\u2022 Providing broadband vouchers to 750,000 selected\n\nschool students to enhance digital literacy among them;\n\n\u2022 Strengthening the Digital Startup Fund of Funds to\n\nattract private investment into Sri Lankan businesses;"
