    "chunk_text": "\u2022 Although approximately 42,000 students are admitted to government universities annually, many students who qualify for university entry are denied this opportunity due to limited resources. With the objective of providing higher education opportunities for these students, the government has implemented a programme, facilitated through State banks, that offers interest-free loans to eligible students, enabling them to pursue degree programs at private higher education institutions. It is proposed to increase the monthly subsistence allowance currently available to these students from Rs. 6,250 to Rs. 10,000, effective from April, 2027.\n\n8.3 Vocational Education\n\nVocational education is being carried out at various levels through various departments and institutions, in more than 550 centres scattered across the country. Rs.\n\n367 368\n\n2026 \u0db1 \u0ddc\u0dc0\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 12\n\n50 million has been allocated to conduct a study on centralizing direction and regulation within a single institution, with the aim of providing quality vocational education and the necessary infrastructure in them, producing the targeted labour force required by the country and utilizing resources productively.\n\n\u2022 In 2027, Rs. 800 million has been allocated for the\n\nRs. 3,380 million project to develop hostel, canteen, laboratory and workshop facilities at the University of Vocational Technology in Ratmalana.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 200 million has been allocated in 2027 for\n\nimproving the infrastructure of institutions belonging to the technical education and training sector, including the German Technical Training Institute and the Automobile Engineering Training Institute.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 1,500 million has been allocated for the year\n\n2027 for the project costing Rs. 6,000 million to modernize 25 selected Technical Colleges in 25 districts."
