    "chunk_text": "\u2022 Preparing national research and development policies\n\nto suit the future needs of the country.\n\n\u2022 Taking new technologies discovered through research to commercialization and integrating them into the country's economy.\n\nSteps will also be taken to provide the institutional, technical and infrastructure facilities necessary to carry out research covering various subject areas through research institutions and other public institutions under various Ministries. Through Government investment, Rs. 23,800 million has been allocated for research and development programmes in 2027.\n\nRs. 7,600 million, including operational expenses, has been allocated to coordinate all such research activities under the Ministry of Science and Technology.\n\nThe National Research and Development Bill has been drafted. It is expected to be presented to Parliament in the first half of 2027.\n\n10. Development of Expressways and Highways\n\nThrough this Budget, we expect to make the largest investment in the development of highways, expressways and railways. Rs. 251 billion has been allocated for this purpose in this Budget. Further, we expect to spend Rs. 487 billion, including Rs. 146 billion as new proposals and Rs. 90 billion from the Ditwah Supplementary Estimate for the restoration of damage caused to railways, highways and bridges by Cyclone \u201cDitwah\u201d. Mainly;\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to allocate Rs. 30,000 million for the\n\nconstruction from Kurunegala to Galewela as the first step of the Kurunegala\u2013Dambulla expressway section, which is the 4th phase of the Central Expressway.\n\n\u2022 An amount of Rs. 18,680 million has been allocated\n\nin 2026 for the initial activities of the development of the first phase of the Ruwanpura Expressway from Kahathuduwa to Ingiriya, and it is proposed to allocate Rs. 27,000 million in 2027.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 53,450 million has been allocated for the year"
