    "chunk_text": "Including these proposals, an investment of Rs. 8,500 million has been allocated for development activities in the youth affairs and sports sector for the year 2027.\n\n20. Social Protection and Empowerment\n\n\u2022 Rs. 230 billion has been allocated in 2027 for social protection allowances, including Aswesuma, to minimize economic hardships and ensure the social protection of the poor and extremely poor groups by continuing to provide them with Aswesuma benefits.\n\n\u2022 The monthly allowance provided to kidney patients will be increased by Rs. 2,500, from Rs. 10,000 to Rs. 12,500.\n\n\u2022 The monthly allowance provided to persons with disabilities will be increased by Rs. 2,500, from Rs. 10,000 to Rs. 12,500.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 25,000 million has been allocated to implement the integrated rural development programme Island-wide under the Praja Shakthi National Movement, giving priority attention to the eradication of poverty.\n\n\u2022 An empowerment pilot project was implemented with the assistance of projects funded by the Asian Development Bank and the World Bank, and Rs. 4,500 million has been allocated for the programme to systematically empower eligible families with potential.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 182 million has been allocated for the holistic personality development of children through a family-centred approach, with the aim of ensuring the protection, health, education and mental well-being of vulnerable children.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 102 million has been allocated for an alternative care structure focused on vulnerable children and children who have lost their parents due to disasters.\n\n\u2022 A Disability Inclusion Focal Point will be established in every Ministry, department and major public institution for the community of persons with disabilities."
