    "md5": "72cb47cde3f77f5b59156b56bb0a1ebb",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1967,
    "chunk_text": "\u2022 It is proposed to allocate Rs. 100 million to extend State patronage for meeting the basic needs of care centres for persons with disabilities run by non-governmental organizations.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to allocate Rs. 500 million to provide facilities for high-capacity children's homes.\n\nSri Lankans Overseas\n\n\u2022 A highly concessionary housing loan scheme of up to Rs. 5 million will be implemented to meet the housing needs of migrant workers. Under this scheme, steps will be taken to provide an interest subsidy of 10 per cent for up to Rs. 3 million and an interest subsidy of 5 per cent for the remaining Rs. 2 million.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed that, for the first Rs. 3 million, a contribution of 6 per cent be borne by the Government and a contribution of 4 per cent by the Sri Lanka Bureau of Foreign Employment, and for the remaining Rs. 2 million, a contribution of 3 per cent be borne by the Government and a contribution of 2 per cent by the Sri Lanka Bureau of Foreign Employment.\n\nIt is proposed to allocate a sum of Rs. 1,000 million in 2027 as the Government contribution for the implementation of this interest subsidy scheme.\n\n21. Disaster Management\n\n\u2022 The installation of a modern Doppler Radar System for highly accurate weather forecasting, received as a JICA grant, will commence in 2027.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 1,000 million has been allocated for the rehabilitation of safe centres to ensure the safety of people during disasters.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 500 million has been allocated to provide disaster response equipment essential for strengthening early warning.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 670 million has been allocated to establish an Island-wide digital radio communication system.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 500 million has been allocated for the rehabilitation of 77 existing coastal early warning towers, the construction of 120 new land-based towers covering flood, landslide and tsunami-prone areas in 25 districts, and the establishment of a multi-hazard early warning communication system."
