    "chunk_index": 461,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "4af178c5698082b10d6d7e4d4aeec149",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1850,
    "chunk_text": "\u2022 A land area of three acres has been identified within the Nuwaragam Forest Reserve in the Anuradhapura District to construct a hospital capable of treating wild animals for animal welfare. It is expected to allocate Rs. 700 million from the Wildlife Fund for the establishment of this hospital.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 50 million has been allocated from the Wildlife Fund for the initial work of constructing a centre for the treatment and rehabilitation of injured marine animals such as turtles and dolphins on a land area of two acres in the Dodanduwa area.\n\nWe expect to further strengthen the legal framework to protect the wild elephant resource, which is a living heritage of Sri Lanka, and to prevent cruelty inflicted on them.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to increase the compensation paid for damage to a house due to the human-elephant conflict from Rs. 200,000 to Rs. 1 million, the compensation paid for a person who dies or\n\n391 392\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd4\u0dbb \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0db8\u0ddc\u0dbb \u0daf\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0ddc \u0ddc\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0ddc ]\n\n2026 \u0db1 \u0ddc\u0dc0\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 12\n\nbecomes fully disabled due to attacks by protected animals, including wild elephants, from Rs. 1 million to Rs. 2 million, the compensation paid for partial disability from Rs. 150,000 to Rs. 500,000, and the compensation paid for other property other than houses from Rs. 200,000 to Rs. 500,000.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to amend the Fauna and Flora Protection Ordinance to increase, in addition to the existing term of imprisonment, the fine for killing, hunting, shooting, wounding or capturing a wild elephant from the current fine of Rs. 150,000 to Rs. 500,000 to Rs. 500,000 to Rs. 1 million. It is proposed to amend the Increase of Fines Act, No. 12 of 2005 to increase the fine for illegally keeping an elephant in possession from the current Rs. 150,000 to Rs. 250,000 to Rs. 500,000 to Rs. 1 million."
  },
