    "chunk_size_bytes": 2005,
    "chunk_text": "\u2022 Under the Government of India loan assistance programme, the work required to rehabilitate the railway section from Rambukkana to Peradeniya, the up-country railway line from Peradeniya to Gampola, and the Matale railway line in a safer and more stable manner, in accordance with modern engineering standards, has commenced. It is expected that trains will be able to operate up to Kandy within the first quarter of 2027.\n\n\u2022 Accordingly, it is expected to fully rehabilitate the Up-Country railway line and restore train operations up to Badulla by the middle of 2027.\n\n\u2022 Under the Cyclone Ditwah damage rehabilitation programme of the Government of China, rehabilitation work on nine bridges located in the Gampaha, Kegalle, Ampara, Kurunegala, Polonnaruwa and Batticaloa Districts has been prepared through a grant for the reconstruction of 14 destroyed bridges.\n\n26. Drinking Water Supply\n\nRs. 77,000 million has been allocated for the uninterrupted supply of clean drinking water to the people, the expansion of sanitation facilities, and the supply of adequate quantities of water for economic activities, including industries. Further, the invitation of private investment is being considered.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 5,190 million has been allocated to commence 13 new projects, including in Jaffna, Mannar, Mullaitivu, Vavuniya, Nagadeepa, Valaichchenai and Kotte, to meet drinking water requirements.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to allocate Rs. 1,800 million for the year 2027 for the commencement of the Kundasale\u2013Haragama Water Supply Project with a cost of Rs. 34,368 million.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to allocate Rs. 1,000 million for the commencement of the Eheliyagoda Water Supply Project with a cost of Rs. 4,775 million.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to allocate Rs. 1,800 million for the commencement of the Greater Kilinochchi Water Supply Project with a cost of Rs. 41,140\n\nmillion, covering the Karachchi, Kandavalai, Poonakary and Pachchilaipalli Divisional Secretary\u2019s Divisions in the Kilinochchi District."
