    "chunk_text": "\u2022 It is proposed to allocate Rs. 1,800 million for the commencement of the Greater Kilinochchi Water Supply Project with a cost of Rs. 41,140\n\nmillion, covering the Karachchi, Kandavalai, Poonakary and Pachchilaipalli Divisional Secretary\u2019s Divisions in the Kilinochchi District.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 700 million has been allocated for the commencement of the Haldummulla\u2013Beragala Water Supply Project with a cost of Rs. 3,262 million.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 300 million has been allocated in 2027 for the commencement of the Yatimahana\u2013Ma Oya Water Supply Project, with a cost of Rs. 22,158 million.\n\n\u2022 Provisions will continuously be provided to resolve step by step the problems relating to drinking water in the Jaffna and the Vanni Districts, such as seawater intrusion, high hardness, high mineral salts and bacterial contamination. It is proposed to allocate Rs. 1,000 million for this purpose.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 12,000 million has been allocated to implement projects, including improving the capacity of existing drinking water projects, expanding distribution and constructing sanitation facilities.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 250 million has been allocated for feasibility studies to meet the water requirements for industrial and commercial activities in the areas of Kuliyapitiya, Pannala, Bingiriya, Udubaddawa, Trincomalee and Gampola\u2013Jayamalapura.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 2,000 million has been allocated for improving community water supply schemes across the Island.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 1,740 million has been allocated to implement the Ella, Moratuwa and Ekala wastewater management projects with the aim of improving sanitation facilities and managing wastewater in a formal manner.\n\n27. Housing and Urban Development\n\nA secure house and a healthy urban environment are the most fundamental basis for the progress of a nation and its human resources. Our expectation is to uplift the living standards of the people by planning economic, social and physical development in an integrated manner, while protecting the natural and built environment."
