    "chunk_text": "\u2022 Rs. 3,200 million has been allocated for projects aimed at improving urban flood control and environmental systems, including the restoration of identified canals in Colombo and its suburban\n\n397 398\n\n\u0db4\u0ddc\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\ncities and the improvement of the stormwater drainage system adjacent to the Piliyandala\u2013Kesbewa by-road.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 900 million has been allocated to carry out a scientific study on the sustainable development of the Beira Lake and the surrounding land use and prepare a development plan, and in the meantime, to implement the essential development activities already identified.\n\n\u2022 I emphasized in the last Budget the need for a sustainable solution for urban flood control. Rs. 250 million was allocated to prepare a short-term, medium-term and long-term plan for this purpose. That plan is currently being prepared.\n\n28. Public Security\n\n\u2022 Rs. 9,500 million has been allocated for the digitalization of the duties of the Sri Lanka Police, the complete modernization of the National Police Academy, the development of the Police Hospital in Narahenpita, the development of the Police Training School in Attidiya, the construction of the Police Sports Complex in Mirihana and the upgrading of facilities and infrastructure at the Special Task Force camps in Gonahena, Kurunegala, Arantalawa, Kegalle and Kirindiwela.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to allocate Rs. 200 million for feasibility studies and the preparation of plans to construct a new administrative building to house in a single building the various divisions of the Sri Lanka Police Department, which are currently operating in buildings obtained on a rental basis at various locations in the City of Colombo, with the aim of providing a more efficient service to the public."
