    "chunk_text": "Severe congestion has arisen within the prison system of our country. Exceeding the capacity to hold around 16,500 persons in 22 prisons and 14 work camps, nearly 36,500 inmates, around twice that number, are currently being held. Officers as well as inmates have lost their lives due to unfortunate incidents that occurred within prisons as a result of this congestion and the drug menace.\n\n399 400\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd4\u0dbb \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0db8\u0ddc\u0dbb \u0daf\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0ddc \u0ddc\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0ddc ]\n\n2026 \u0db1 \u0ddc\u0dc0\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 12\n\n\u2022 In line with the Galle Heritage City Development Plan and tourism zone promotion activities, it is proposed to allocate a sum of Rs. 500 million in this Budget for the commencement of the relocation of the current Galle Prison from its location to the Boossa area.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 1,000 million has been allocated for the expansion of the Wariyapola and Watareka Prisons, where development work has already commenced, to increase their holding capacity.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 500 million has been allocated for the relocation of the Matara Prison to the Kotawilawatta area in Matara.\n\n30. National Security\n\n\u2022 Provisions of Rs. 250 million have been allocated for the establishment of a Defence Development Research Centre, affiliated to the Ministry of Defence, for research carried out by the security forces.\n\n\u2022 There are teams in the security forces recruited for construction work. It is proposed to provide a special allowance to these personnel when they are deployed in various development programmes of the Government.\n\n\u2022 As a tribute to the parents of war heroes who joined the armed forces before 2009, it is proposed that the Ministry of Defence expeditiously prepare a programme to increase the monthly allowance of Rs. 750 currently paid to the mother and father and to implement it from July, 2027."
