    "chunk_text": "\u2022 Various programmes are being implemented, including: the provision and sustainable maintenance of physical infrastructure, such as \u201cHaritha Mawatha,\u201d \u201cClean Colombo,\u201d \u201cClean Islands,\u201d \u201cClean City,\u201d \u201cClean Sri Lanka-Aththama,\u201d the modernization of 'Dream Destination' railway stations, and the establishment of standardized public sanitation facilities; environmental development projects, including the creation of elephant nourishment zones; and initiatives to promote positive public habits, community participation, and corporate responsibility.\n\n\u2022 The Clean Island project, proposed to be implemented with the support of the Ministry of Energy, will develop the islands of Delft, Nainativu and Analaitivu as \u201cmodel islands\u201d for integrated development and transformation.\n\n34. Public Administration and Public Services\n\n\u2022 A four-year project will be implemented to enhance the revenue-generating capacity of Local Government Institutions, utilize existing resources productively and strengthen financial sustainability. Through this, it is expected to continuously maintain the essential services of Local Government Institutions, and provision of Rs. 1,000 million has been allocated for this purpose.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to provide provisions of Rs. 575 million from Provincial Council funds to complete the construction of the Capital Square building, which was commenced by the Kurunegala Municipal Council and abandoned without being completed.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to allocate provisions of Rs. 50,000 million at Rs. 2,000 million per District to implement the District Development Programme and the Decentralized Budget Programme. Of this, Rs. 47,750 million will be allocated for special development programmes identified at District level, and the remaining Rs. 2,250 million for implementing the Decentralized Budget Programme at Rs. 10 million per Member of Parliament."
