    "chunk_text": "\u2022 It is proposed to allocate provisions of Rs. 50,000 million at Rs. 2,000 million per District to implement the District Development Programme and the Decentralized Budget Programme. Of this, Rs. 47,750 million will be allocated for special development programmes identified at District level, and the remaining Rs. 2,250 million for implementing the Decentralized Budget Programme at Rs. 10 million per Member of Parliament.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 1,100 million has been allocated for the construction of new District Secretariat offices in the Vavuniya, Puttalam and Anuradhapura districts with the aim of providing an efficient and quality public service to the public.\n\n\u2022 Rs. 265 million has been allocated for the commencement of the construction of new Divisional Secretariat office buildings in Dehiattakandiya and Elapatha to further formalize public services at the regional level.\n\n403 404\n\n2026 \u0db1 \u0ddc\u0dc0\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 12\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to introduce a fairer and simpler mechanism, effective from the year 2027, to address the difficulties arising from the current system which limits the allocation of funds for salaries in Local Government Institutions to 20 per cent and 40 per cent. Accordingly, it is proposed to cover 100 per cent of the funding required for staff salary expenditures in 46 financially weak Local Government Authorities in 2027. It is also proposed to change these percentages for the other Local Government Institutions. Furthermore, Rs. 1,750 million has been allocated to support capital programmes, based on plans submitted by these institutions.\n\n\u2022 Provisions of Rs. 1,100 million have been allocated to complete the construction of the Kegalle and Nuwara Eliya District Secretariat offices and the Negombo, Homagama, Kalutara, Pitabeddara, Angunakolapelessa and Deraniyagala Divisional Secretariat offices, work on which has already commenced, in order to enhance the efficiency of public officers and provide a quality service to the public."
