    "chunk_text": "\u2022 Provisions of Rs. 1,100 million have been allocated to complete the construction of the Kegalle and Nuwara Eliya District Secretariat offices and the Negombo, Homagama, Kalutara, Pitabeddara, Angunakolapelessa and Deraniyagala Divisional Secretariat offices, work on which has already commenced, in order to enhance the efficiency of public officers and provide a quality service to the public.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to resolve the issues existing within departmental services and other executive services, in alignment with the promotion mechanisms currently in place for Island-wide services.\n\n\u2022 In order to provide adequate human resources for maintaining an efficient and quality public service in public institutions, approval has already been granted by the Officials' Committee on Staff Management appointed by the Cabinet of Ministers and the Department of Management Services for recruitment to 148,940 vacancies, while reviewing the recruitment process of the Public Service. Of this number, around 40,000 recruitments have been completed so far, and provisions will be allocated to recruit a further 110,000 in the future.\n\n\u2022 The Sethsiripaya Stage III Project in Battaramulla has commenced. This project is expected to be completed in 2028, and Rs. 6,800 million has been allocated for this purpose.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to implement the Sethsiripaya Stage IV Project, with a day care centre, at Denzil Kobbekaduwa Mawatha, Battaramulla, by deploying the funds of the Urban Development Authority.\n\n35. Public Sector Salaries and Pensions\n\nHon. Speaker, through our first Budget in 2025, steps were taken to increase the basic salary by increasing the minimum monthly basic salary of the public sector by Rs. 15,750 and by increasing the value of the annual salary"
