    "md5": "275924239d41fcff8589ca10bba50967",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1850,
    "chunk_text": "\u2022 With the aim of encouraging the use of electric vehicles, it is proposed to increase by 150 per cent, with effect from July, 2027, the monthly allowance paid in terms of Public Administration Circular 13/2008(V) to officers entitled to an official vehicle and who use fully electric private vehicles.\n\nAllowances in the Health Sector\n\n\u2022 To strengthen the national health system, it is proposed to increase the monthly special duty allowance of nursing officers and officers in the paramedical and supplementary medical services from Rs. 6,000 to Rs. 12,000, and the monthly special duty allowance of other health staff from Rs. 2,000 to Rs. 4,000.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to pay the above allowance increases proposed for the health sector in two steps. Accordingly, 50 per cent of the increase will be paid from July 2027, and the remaining 50 per cent in 2028.\n\n405 406\n\n\u0db4\u0ddc\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nPayments to Lecturers in Universities and Vocational Training Institutes\n\n\u2022 Considering the important role played by university academic staff in improving the quality of higher education, promoting research activities and developing human resources, it is proposed to increase the monthly academic allowance currently paid to such staff by Rs. 25,000. It is expected to pay 50 per cent of this increase from July, 2027, and the remaining 50 per cent from July, 2028.\n\n\u2022 In order to attract external lecturers with specialist knowledge to universities for academic activities, it is proposed to increase the payments made to external lecturers threefold in line with the existing rates. Accordingly, it is proposed to increase the allowance currently paid per hour from Rs. 1,500 to Rs. 4,500. Further, it is proposed to increase the allowance of Rs. 600 paid per hour to external advisers for practical examinations to Rs. 1,800."
