    "chunk_text": "\u2022 In order to attract external lecturers with specialist knowledge to universities for academic activities, it is proposed to increase the payments made to external lecturers threefold in line with the existing rates. Accordingly, it is proposed to increase the allowance currently paid per hour from Rs. 1,500 to Rs. 4,500. Further, it is proposed to increase the allowance of Rs. 600 paid per hour to external advisers for practical examinations to Rs. 1,800.\n\nFood Allowance of the Tri-Forces\n\n\u2022 Considering the increase in the cost incurred for the food of members of the tri-forces, and with the aim of meeting their nutritional requirements and ensuring their welfare, it is proposed to increase the daily food allowance paid to the tri-forces, with effect from July, 2027, by Rs. 315 for officers and by Rs. 332 for other ranks.\n\nFood and Accommodation Allowance of Officers of the Sri Lanka Police\n\n\u2022 Considering the increase in food and accommodation expenses that police officers have to bear in the performance of their duties, it is proposed to increase the monthly food and accommodation allowance currently paid to meet such expenses by Rs. 10,000 with effect from July, 2027.\n\nRisk Allowance for Prison Officers\n\n\u2022 Taking into account the difficult and high-risk working conditions faced by prison officers in the performance of their duties, steps will be taken to increase the monthly risk allowance currently paid by 100 per cent, from Rs. 8,000 to Rs. 16,000.\n\n\u2022 Likewise, it is proposed to increase the allowance of Rs. 2,250 currently paid to civil officers serving in the Department of Prisons to Rs. 10,000.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to pay these proposed allowances of officers serving in the Department of Prisons with effect from July, 2027.\n\nAllowances for Field Officers"
