    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "8b614f0d15fc640a8672fb225443aad7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1916,
    "chunk_text": "\u2022 The Government is implementing a phased pension revision programme with the objective of ensuring a fair and structured pension system for all pensioners by systematically eliminating the disparities that exist among the pensions of retired public servants.\n\n\u2022 It is also the objective of the Government to minimize and eliminate in phases, taking into account sustainable public financial management, the disparity that has arisen, due to the new basic salary revision implemented in 2025, between the pensions of public servants who retired before 2025 and those retiring in or after 2025.\n\n\u2022 It is proposed to provide a monthly interim allowance of Rs. 2,500, with effect from 01, July 2027, as a relief to pensioners who retired during the period from 2020 to 2024, until the pension revision scheduled to be carried out under the new 2025 basic salary structure is implemented.\n\n\u2022 The forthcoming pension revision based on the new 2025 basic salary structure is planned to commence with the 2028 Budget and to be implemented in several phases. Once this\n\n409 410\n\n\u0db4\u0ddc\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dd2\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nrevision is applied to the relevant pensioners and the payment of the revised pension commences, the payment of the above-mentioned monthly interim allowance of Rs. 2,500 proposed for those who retired during the period 2020\u20132024 will cease.\n\n\u2022 These provisions will also apply to public sector pensioners whose salaries were determined under Department of Management Services Circulars 02/2025, 03/2025, 04/2025 and 05/2025.\n\n\u2022 The overall objective of all these measures is to provide fair relief to public servants who retired at different times by systematically narrowing the pension disparities among them, and to establish a sustainable pension system in the long term.\n\n36. Tax Policy Proposals\n\n36.1 Increasing the Personal Income Tax Relief\n\nand Revising the Progressive Tax Slabs"
