    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "c9ea939c7e9bf71786ff47f88cb53f78",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1855,
    "chunk_text": "Hon. Speaker, the supply of bunker fuel to ships engaged in international transport is an important component of Sri Lanka's maritime services sector. This industry operates in a highly competitive international market.\n\n36.8 Review and Rationalization of the Tax\n\nStructure applicable to the Betting and Gaming Industry\n\nHon. Speaker, addressing the long-standing need for an effective regulatory framework for the betting and gaming industry, the Government has established the Gambling Regulatory Authority \u2013 GRA - and commenced its operations.\n\nGiven that a regulatory framework is now in place, it is proposed to conduct a comprehensive review of the taxes, fees, and charges applicable to this industry with the view to eliminate instances of double taxation and inconsistencies, align the tax structure with international best practices, and ensure a fair and balanced approach that supports the sustainable development of the industry while safeguarding government revenue.\n\nThis review aims to establish a simple, transparent, and integrated tax structure that is easy to administer and facilitates compliance.\n\n36.9 Strengthening Tax Administration and Facilitating Taxpayer Compliance\n\nHon. Speaker, with the objective of strengthening tax administration, enhancing legal certainty, and facilitating tax compliance for taxpayers, we propose to remove\n\nambiguities present in certain provisions of existing tax laws. Furthermore, we propose to review and amend these provisions to align them with evolving business practices and new forms of transactions.\n\nAdditionally, we propose to review certain stringent procedural requirements which could lead to taxpayers denied legitimate tax refunds or input tax credits due technical or procedural noncompliance while ensuring that adequate safeguards remain in place to protect government revenue."
