    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/24650_english_2026-11-12.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-11-12-2026-11-12-0493",
    "chunk_index": 493,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "3717217af6ef826b596c2bbde3a96ff1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1934,
    "chunk_text": "The borrowing limit of the Appropriation Bill for the financial year 2027 is presented in Annexure IV. Summary of New Expenditure Proposals Presented in the 2027 Budget is given in Annexure II. Further, the documents to be presented with the Second Reading of the Budget under the Public Financial Management Act, No. 44 of 2024 have also been tabled.\n\n38. Supplementary Estimate for Ditwah Reconstruction \u2013 2027\n\nAccordingly, in addition to the 2027 Budget I have presented, it is proposed to present to Parliament a Supplementary Estimate for Ditwah reconstruction expenditure in accordance with the provisions of Section 16 of the Public Financial Management Act.\n\nIt is proposed to table that Supplementary Estimate today, following the Budget Speech.\n\nConclusion\n\nHon. Speaker, our Budget Proposals are not confined to paper alone. They are Proposals that are implemented in practice on the ground. Therefore, every new proposal will have a clearly accountable institution, outcome indicators, national priorities, a cash flow plan and transparency that can be easily observed by the public.\n\nWhat we are striving to build is a country that safeguards the dignity of the citizen, ensures the safety of the child, gives due value to labour, creates opportunities for knowledge and protects natural resources for future generations.\n\nHaving overcome the challenges that prevailed and built stability in the economy, our next target is to commence a forward-looking and transformative era in 2027. For this, the collective strength and contribution of all of you is essential to us.\n\nHon. Speaker, in the modern world, governments are changed through progressive ideological revolutions, through the intelligent decisions of the people and through advanced policies and programmes suited to the future. However, our Opposition is still clinging to superstitious beliefs and has been unable to free itself from regressive thinking."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-12-2026-11-12",
    "num": "2026-11-12",
    "date_str": "2026-11-12",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-11-12",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/24650_english_2026-11-12.pdf",
