    "chunk_index": 494,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "a1a7b4db520e4ec7a21cb96ac083f22c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1649,
    "chunk_text": "Hon. Speaker, in the modern world, governments are changed through progressive ideological revolutions, through the intelligent decisions of the people and through advanced policies and programmes suited to the future. However, our Opposition is still clinging to superstitious beliefs and has been unable to free itself from regressive thinking.\n\nLikewise, read the Kalama Sutta, which the Lord Buddha preached to the Kalamas -the residents of the town of Kesaputta-, pointing out that nothing should be accepted blindly but should be examined with wisdom, and understand the revolution the Lord Buddha made against blind faith. Read the Agga\u00f1\u00f1a Sutta, which the Lord Buddha preached against superstition, and the Kevatta Sutta, preached against false incantations, and understand the ideological revolution brought about by the Lord Buddha.\n\nIn the Tevijja Sutta, the Lord Buddha asks whether, if a man standing on this bank of a river, wishing to go to the other bank, neither swims nor uses a boat but prays to the far bank, saying \"Come here, far bank, come here\", the far bank would come to this side.\n\nHon. Speaker, we have a very clear, progressive and proud dream for our Motherland. Our hope is to make this country not merely an island, but one of the most advanced countries, not only in Asia but in the whole world, rich in knowledge, skills and modern technology.\n\nToday, we are implementing a strong programme towards that end. We have commenced thetransformationofmaking ouryoungergeneration andour children across the country fully skilled, advanced citizens by providing them with modern technology, science and global knowledge."
