    "md5": "8511162a9393933d691cd633257a5b36",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2062,
    "chunk_text": "Today, we are implementing a strong programme towards that end. We have commenced thetransformationofmaking ouryoungergeneration andour children across the country fully skilled, advanced citizens by providing them with modern technology, science and global knowledge.\n\n415 416\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd4\u0dbb \u0d9a\u0dd4\u0db8\u0ddc\u0dbb \u0daf\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0ddc \u0ddc\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0ddc ]\n\n2026 \u0db1 \u0ddc\u0dc0\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 12\n\nwith a unique intelligence. We want to prove to the whole world that we have a generation of citizens who fulfil the responsibilities they have undertaken, work with dedication, create new ideas, find solutions in the face of challenges and can move forward shoulder to shoulder with the world. What we are trying to build is not only a new economy for Sri Lanka, but also a new recognition, a new respect and a new pride for the Sri Lankan before the world.\n\nHon. Speaker, criticize the Government. Question our policies. Present a better alternative programme than ours. We fully accept your democratic right to do so. But bring alternative policies instead of curse verses, creative solutions instead of sorcery, and intelligent dialogue instead of yaga and homa rituals into the politics of this country. When the people of our country are moving forward with technology and intelligence, should the politics of the Opposition alone turn upside down and go backwards? I would like to remind at this moment that building a political culture that befits the civilized, enlightened and proud Sri Lankan identity we are trying to build before the world is a fundamental responsibility entrusted not only to the Government, but also to the Opposition. The intelligent people of this country will never again set foot in that old darkness.\n\nHon. Speaker, what we must leave behind for future generations is not our party disputes, but a prosperous and just country the future of which they can take over with confidence. Therefore, let us make the name \"Sri Lankan\" not merely a name we pronounce with pride, but a proud name that the whole world accepts with respect."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-11-12-2026-11-12",
